#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-beasth7AIO.rst:91
#: 09bc093ca9304aa9a64c451690e93520
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-beasth7AIO.rst:93
#: f35c06d4f14647d28643e2f748d82258
msgid "RC input is configured by default via the USART3 RX input. It supports all RC protocols except PPM. FPort and full duplex protocols will need to use instead,both RX1 and TX1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-beasth7AIO.rst:95
#: 7ccd49ba287745d2bf51698832460791
msgid "If the receiver is FPort or a full duplex protocol, then the receiver must be tied to the USART1 TX pin and :ref:`SERIAL1_OPTIONS<SERIAL1_OPTIONS>` = 7 (invert TX/RX, half duplex), :ref:`SERIAL1_PROTOCOL<SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>` set to 23, and :ref:`RSSI_TYPE<RSSI_TYPE>` =3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-beasth7AIO.rst:99
#: bcefb5d548304330aad00dcbb1d666aa
msgid "Dshot Capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-iflight-beasth7AIO.rst:101
#: 863923acd1f9499097935075b6f2fc42
msgid "All motor 1-4 outputs are bi-directional Dshot and PWM capable. However, mixing Dshot and normal PWM operation for outputs is restricted into groups, ie. enabling Dshot for an output in a group requires that ALL outputs in that group be configured and used as Dshot, rather than PWM outputs. The output groups that must be the same (PWM rate or Dshot, when configured as a normal servo/motor output) are: 1/4, and 2/3."
msgstr ""

